WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nmm_131'), 'CourseService caches course outlines in memory for 10 minutes; CourseController calls courseService.invalidate(courseId) after an admin edits a course with PATCH /courses/:id. EnrollmentModule failed at startup because CourseService was missing, and this fix was merged:

// src/enrollments/enrollment.module.ts
 @Module({
   controllers: [EnrollmentController],
-  providers: [EnrollmentService, EnrollmentRepository],
+  providers: [EnrollmentService, EnrollmentRepository, CourseService, CourseRepository],
 })
 export class EnrollmentModule {}

// src/courses/course.module.ts (unchanged)
@Module({
  controllers: [CourseController],
  providers: [CourseService, CourseRepository],
  exports: [CourseService],
})
export class CourseModule {}

Statement: "After this fix, when an admin marks two lessons of course 42 as previews with PATCH /courses/42, the price quote from EnrollmentService uses the new outline right away."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. A class listed in the providers of two modules becomes two providers: Nest creates one CourseService for CourseModule and another for EnrollmentModule, each with its own cache. PATCH /courses/42 goes through CourseController and invalidates the cache of CourseModule''s instance only; EnrollmentService keeps quoting from its own instance''s stale outline for up to 10 minutes. The right fix is imports: [CourseModule] in EnrollmentModule (CourseModule already exports CourseService), which gives EnrollmentService the same instance that CourseController uses. The misconception is that a provider is a single global object no matter where it is declared: sharing comes from exporting and importing, not from naming the class twice.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nmm_131') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
