    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nmm_131'), 'ProgressService and its controller:

@Injectable()
export class ProgressService {
  private currentUserId?: string;
  setUser(userId: string) { this.currentUserId = userId; }

  async complete(lessonId: string) {
    await this.courses.getOutlineForLesson(lessonId);          // about 25 ms
    await this.progress.insert(this.currentUserId!, lessonId);
  }
}

@Post(":id/complete")
async complete(@Param("id") lessonId: string, @Req() req: AuthenticatedRequest) {
  this.progressService.setUser(req.user.id);
  return this.progressService.complete(lessonId);
}

API log:
10:41:07.112 POST /lessons/l_301/complete user=u_12
10:41:07.115 POST /lessons/l_877/complete user=u_95
10:41:07.140 lesson_progress insert user=u_95 lesson=l_301
10:41:07.142 lesson_progress insert user=u_95 lesson=l_877

Statement: "ProgressService has the default scope, so one instance serves both requests: the second request''s setUser overwrote currentUserId during the first request''s await, and lesson l_301 was recorded for the wrong learner."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Without a scope option, a provider is a singleton: one ProgressService for the whole application. Request 1 sets currentUserId to u_12 and waits about 25 ms for the outline; 3 ms later request 2 sets the same field to u_95; when request 1 resumes, it reads u_95, which is exactly what the log shows. The fix is to keep per-request data out of singleton fields: complete(userId, lessonId) with the controller passing req.user.id. Scope.REQUEST would also stop the mix-up, but it creates a new service, controller and dependency chain for every request, so it is the expensive answer to a problem an argument solves. The misconception is that each HTTP request gets its own service objects by default.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nmm_131') AND order_index = 3)
    RETURNING id
)
