Statement: "The string \"false\" passed @IsBoolean() because class-transformer converted it to true before the validators ran."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. ValidationPipe first turns the plain body into an EnrollDto instance with class-transformer, then runs class-validator on that instance. With enableImplicitConversion, class-transformer converts each value to the property''s reflected type, and for a boolean that is `Boolean(value)`: any non-empty string, "false" included, becomes true. @IsBoolean() then sees a real boolean and passes. The safe options are to leave implicit conversion off for JSON bodies (JSON already has booleans and numbers, so a client that sends a string has sent the wrong type), or to write an explicit @Transform that accepts only "true" and "false". The misconception is that the validator sees what the client sent; it sees what the transformer produced.', 2, 5
