Statement: "With this test in CI, the endpoint stays safe as the users table grows, because any leak would make the test fail."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The handler returns the whole row minus one named field, so every column added later is published by default: after the migration the response contains mfaSecret, and the test still passes because it only checks the one field somebody remembered. That is a deny-list. The safe shape is an allow-list: map the entity to a response DTO that names exactly the public fields (id, displayName, avatarUrl, joinedAt), and test the exact set of keys (`expect(Object.keys(res).sort()).toEqual([...])`), which fails as soon as anything new appears. The misconception is that a test for the known leak protects against the next one.', 1, 5
