VALUES ('chal_coding_nmm_222', (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'nestjs-modular-monolith'), (SELECT id FROM course.module WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'nestjs-modular-monolith') AND order_index = 2 AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), (SELECT id FROM course.lesson WHERE content_source = 'lesson-nmm-2-2' AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), 'thin-controller-handlers', 'Write thin controller handlers', 'Two CodeDev controllers had drifted (each held its own copy of an enrollment rule) and GET /users/:id/profile returned a whole user row, passwordHash included. The service is now the only place for rules; your job is the controller around it. The starter contains CatalogService (already written, do not change) and an empty CodeDevController with three handlers. A request is { params, query, body, user } with string query and params values; a response is { status, headers, body }. Each handler maps the request, calls the service once, and maps the result; a 400 never calls the service. listCourses (GET /courses): query page (default 1) and limit (default 20) must be digits only and at least 1, otherwise 400 "page must be a positive integer" / "limit must be a positive integer"; a limit above 50 becomes 50; level is optional and must be exactly "beginner", "intermediate" or "advanced", otherwise 400 "level must be one of: beginner, intermediate, advanced"; check page, limit, level in that order. Call service.listCourses({ page, limit, level }) and answer 200 with headers { "X-Total-Count": String(total) } and body { items: [{ id, title, level, priceVnd }], page, limit, total }. enroll (POST /enrollments): the body must be an object (not null, not an array) whose courseId is a string, otherwise 400 "courseId is required"; the learner is req.user.id, never a userId sent in the body; call service.enroll({ userId, courseId }) and answer 201 with headers { Location: "/enrollments/<id>" } and body { id, courseId, status, createdAt }. getProfile (GET /users/:id/profile): call service.getProfile(req.params.id); null is 404 with body { error: "user not found" }; otherwise 200 with body { id, displayName, avatarUrl, joinedAt } where joinedAt is the user''s createdAt. Every 400 has headers {} and body { error: "<message>" }; 200 and 404 from getProfile have headers {}. Bodies contain exactly the listed fields: never passwordHash, email, role, internalNotes, paymentRef, published or authorPayoutPercent. Input (stdin): { courses? | generateCourses?, users?, requests: [{ route, query?, params?, body?, user? }] }. For each request the runner prints the request, the response with JSON keys sorted, and the service calls your handler made.', 'open', 'medium'::difficulty_question, 'mini_coding', 30, true, false)
