WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nmm_311'), 'A reactivation path added by a teammate:

async enroll(userId: string, courseId: string) {
  const course = await this.requireCourse(courseId);
  const current = await this.enrollments.findByUserAndCourse(userId, courseId);
  if (current?.status === "active") return { outcome: "existing", enrollment: current };
  if (current?.status === "cancelled") {
    // they were allowed in once
    const reactivated = { ...current, status: "active" as const };
    await this.enrollments.save(reactivated);
    return { outcome: "reactivated", enrollment: reactivated };
  }
  this.assertPublished(course);
  await this.assertPrerequisites(userId, course);
  await this.assertEntitlement(userId, course);
  // ... create
}

Data for learner u_5002: an enrollment in the premium course nestjs-modular-monolith with status "cancelled" since a refund on 2026-09-30, and no entitlement row since then.

Statement: "Reactivating here without checking the entitlement again is safe, because u_5002 passed every rule when the enrollment was first created."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The rules describe the state at the time of the request, not at the time of the first enrollment. Since then u_5002 was refunded and lost the entitlement, so this path gives the premium course back for free. The same applies to a course that was unpublished, or that gained a prerequisite, after the learner cancelled. A reactivation is a new decision: run the published, prerequisite and entitlement checks first, then flip the status of the existing row, which keeps one row per learner and course. The only request that may skip the rules is a repeat of one that already succeeded, which is what returning an active enrollment does. The misconception is treating "was allowed once" as "is allowed now".', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nmm_311') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
