Statement: "Adding PgEnrollmentRepository, which implements EnrollmentRepository, to the providers array of EnrollmentModule fixes this error, because Nest matches the interface to the class that implements it."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. TypeScript interfaces do not exist at runtime. Nest finds constructor dependencies through the type metadata the compiler emits, and for an interface the emitted type is Object, which is exactly what the error message names: "the argument Object at index [0]". Nest never sees EnrollmentRepository, so it cannot match it to a class, however many classes implement it. The fix is a token: export const ENROLLMENT_REPOSITORY = Symbol("ENROLLMENT_REPOSITORY"), register { provide: ENROLLMENT_REPOSITORY, useClass: PgEnrollmentRepository } and inject it with @Inject(ENROLLMENT_REPOSITORY). The misconception is that `implements` creates a link Nest can use; it is a compile-time check only.', 2, 5
