Statement: "The `as UpdateProfileDto` cast removes isAdmin, role and exp from the object at runtime, so the extra columns must have been written by some other code path."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. A type assertion only tells the compiler what shape to assume; TypeScript erases it, and the emitted JavaScript is `return { ok: true, dto: input }`. The object passed to the repository is the parsed request body with every key the client sent, and the repository writes every key it receives - which is exactly what the audit log shows. To remove fields, code has to build a new object from the allowed fields (or ValidationPipe with whitelist has to strip them). The misconception is that TypeScript types filter or check data at runtime; they never run.', 1, 5
