Request: PATCH /users/me/profile
{"displayName":"Minh","isAdmin":true}

Statement: "This request gets 400 Bad Request with the message "property isAdmin should not exist", and the controller method never runs."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. With whitelist: true, ValidationPipe treats every property without a validation decorator as not allowed; forbidNonWhitelisted: true turns that into an error instead of silently stripping it. The pipe runs before the handler, so the request ends with 400 and a message array containing "property isAdmin should not exist", and updateProfile() is never called. With whitelist: true alone, isAdmin would be stripped and the request would succeed with only displayName. The misconception is that declaring a DTO class is enough: the global pipe options decide what happens to unknown properties.', 2, 5
