Statement: "If a later change removed CourseModule from the imports of EnrollmentModule, this test would fail at compile(), even though both repositories are fakes."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. compile() builds the real module graph with Nest''s container and resolves every constructor, exactly as the running app does. The overrides only swap the two repositories; EnrollmentService still needs CourseService, and without the CourseModule import that provider is not visible in the EnrollmentModule context, so compile() throws "Nest can''t resolve dependencies of the EnrollmentService (EnrollmentRepository, ?)". The same test fails if CourseModule stops exporting CourseService or if a module cycle appears. The misconception is that a test with fakes cannot catch wiring errors: a unit test built with new cannot, a testing-module test can.', 1, 5
